        "original_id": "273bca4c-d2bf-5884-aa72-8c1c9fdda9f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Elvey, Arthur Lubin, Arturo de Cordova, Dorothy Patrick, Marjorie Lord\n- Works: Room in the House, New Orleans, Phantom of the Opera, Francis the Talking Mule, Mister Ed, Abbott & Costello films\n- Roles: Film directors, producer, actors\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Elvey was born on 11 November 1887 and died on 28 August 1967.\n- Maurice Elvey was the most prolific film director in British history.\n- Arthur Lubin was born on July 25, 1898 and died on May 12, 1995.\n- Arthur Lubin was an American film director and producer.\n- Arthur Lubin directed several Abbott & Costello films, Phantom of the Opera (1943), and the Francis the Talking Mule series.\n- Arthur Lubin created the talking-horse TV series Mister Ed.\n- Room in the House is a 1955 comedy-drama film directed by Maurice Elvey.\n- The film New Orleans was directed by Arthur Lubin and stars Arturo de Cordova and Dorothy Patrick.\n- The film New Orleans features Marjorie Lord.",
